„­bible_version£KJV¤book§chapter¨sections–…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙØThere was also a lot for the tribe of Manasseh; for he was the firstborn of Joseph; to wit, for Machir the firstborn of Manasseh, the father of Gilead: because he was a man of war, therefore he had Gilead and Bashan.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚ\There was also a lot for the rest of the children of Manasseh by their families; for the children of Abiezer, and for the children of Helek, and for the children of Asriel, and for the children of Shechem, and for the children of Hepher, and for the children of Shemida: these were the male children of Manasseh the son of Joseph by their families.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÑBut Zelophehad, the son of Hepher, the son of Gilead, the son of Machir, the son of Manasseh, had no sons, but daughters: and these are the names of his daughters, Mahlah, and Noah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Tirzah.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚ)And they came near before Eleazar the priest, and before Joshua the son of Nun, and before the princes, saying, The LORD commanded Moses to give us an inheritance among our brethren. Therefore according to the commandment of the LORD he gave them an inheritance among the brethren of their father.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsAnd there fell ten portions to Manasseh, beside the land of Gilead and Bashan, which were on the other side Jordan;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|because the daughters of Manasseh had an inheritance among his sons: and the rest of Manasseh's sons had the land of Gilead.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse
¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¢And the coast of Manasseh was from Asher to Michmethah, that lieth before Shechem; and the border went along on the right hand unto the inhabitants of En-tappuah.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpNow Manasseh had the land of Tappuah: but Tappuah on the border of Manasseh belonged to the children of Ephraim;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙçand the coast descended unto the river Kanah, southward of the river: these cities of Ephraim are among the cities of Manasseh: the coast of Manasseh also was on the north side of the river, and the outgoings of it were at the sea:¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¡southward it was Ephraim's, and northward it was Manasseh's, and the sea is his border; and they met together in Asher on the north, and in Issachar on the east.¦layout ªlast_verse
